# pam-gnupg: keygrips whose passphrase to preset into gpg-agent at the
# start of every login session.  Deployed via home-dotfiles-service-type.
#
# Pre-condition: the GPG passphrase for each listed keygrip MUST equal
# the user's login password for the preset to actually unlock the key.
# Mismatched keygrips are silently skipped — pinentry would still fire
# if/when those keys are used.
#
# To regenerate the list:
#   gpg --list-secret-keys --with-keygrip
#
# Primary key 6513C7248D7BECE2EC1BD34B70350DAD507FA72F is offline (sec#)
# and intentionally not preset.

# [S] sign subkey
2736BEE5BDF5EE673B4E9D17980B111BBF62CD1D
# [E] encrypt subkey — used by `pass` for OAuth tokens, mail creds, etc.
BD945B94486B2F9AF056463067A79E02DBD6B7DA
# [SA] sign+auth subkey
438B15F7C4B3A7FEC1561FD9EFF9C7E85A6FE362
# [A] auth subkeys (SSH)
0FAACBA7A6363ACADF80DB1C88CE02702DFCB8BE
A95146C1DB21F12A646FA046E5C86C5FA7BA6802
79ABE6B512A1FAC7C80718ACA96741C542057036
